@startuml

start

:Integrated avionics stack (FMS/FADEC) hosted on deterministic RTOS for redundancy;
:Execute control laws via high-priority ISRs and lower-frequency worker tasks;

fork
  :Dedicated monitoring task scheduled with real-time priority;
  :Continuously sample from protected ring buffers;
 fork
  :Flight attitude;
 fork again
  :Engine parameters;
 end fork
fork again
  :BMS/PMIC monitor task uses cyclic executive model;
 fork
  :Track fuel consumption;
 fork again
  :Track remaining volume;
 end fork
end fork

if (Altitude breaches safety threshold?) then (yes)
  :Trigger auditory alarm;
  if (Uncorrected within defined window?) then (yes)
    :FADEC engages automatic recovery function;
    :Command aircraft to safe altitude;
  else(no)
  end if

  :Telemetry task handles concurrent updates;
  :Stream via CRC-secured CAN bus/similar data link to ground control station;
else (no)
end if

:Restore normal altitude;
fork
:Silence alarm;
:Log event;
fork again
  :Same RTOS but lower priority navigation management task;
  :Use active flight plan and live meteorological data;
  :Periodically calculate optimal flight path and ETA;
  :Employ exponential backoff for comms faults;
end fork

repeat
  :Periodic monitoring driven by timer interrupts with bounded retries;
  :Ensure flight parameter integrity;
repeat while(Mission completion) is(no)

:In compliance with DO-178C/DO-254;
:Log comprehensive event traces;

if (Detect anomalies ?) then (yes)
  :Initiate fault-tolerant strategies;
  :Immediate data uplink to ground station;
else (no)
end if

stop

@enduml
